.TH smi-pki-do-client-cert-request "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-do-client-cert-request \- Create the private key and certificate request of a client certificate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-do-client-cert-request
.I DIRECTORY CLIENT_NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Creates, in \fIDIRECTORY\fR, a 2048-bit RSA private key \fICLIENT_NAME\fB.client.priv.key\fR (mode \fB600\fR), its public key \fB.client.pub.key\fR and the certificate signing request \fB.client.csr\fR with \fICLIENT_NAME\fR as Common Name.
The other subject fields come from \fIDIRECTORY\fB/subject.sh\fR when it exists (COUNTRY, STATE, LOCALITY, ORG, ORG_UNIT, EMAIL), so a customer names its own organization.
.PP
Run it on the client side and send only the \fB.client.csr\fR file to the CA; keep the private key.
\fICLIENT_NAME\fR must be the name agreed with the CA, because the CA signs only a request whose Common Name is exactly that name.
It is a thin command line wrapper over the matching function in the file based PKI library
\fBpki.sh\fR, so each step of building a CA and signing certificates can be run and inspected
on its own. All material is passed as file names; the command fails if the underlying OpenSSL
operation fails.
.SH MUTUAL TLS WORKFLOW
.IP 1. 4
The client runs \fBsmi-pki-do-client-cert-request\fR \fIDIRECTORY CLIENT_NAME\fR on its own machine,
with the agreed \fICLIENT_NAME\fR, and sends only \fICLIENT_NAME\fB.client.csr\fR. The private key never
leaves the client.
.IP 2. 4
The CA side saves the request as \fIDIRECTORY\fB/\fICLIENT_NAME\fB.client.csr\fR, may inspect it with
\fBsmi-pki-verify-client-csr\fR, and signs it with \fBsmi-pki-do-client-signing\fR
\fIDIRECTORY CLIENT_NAME ROOT_DOMAIN\fR.
.IP 3. 4
The CA side sends back \fICLIENT_NAME\fB.client.chain.crt\fR, and the Root CA certificate
\fBca/\fIROOT_DOMAIN\fB.crt\fR when the client does not have it yet.
.IP 4. 4
The server trusts the CA, for example nginx \fBssl_client_certificate\fR with the Root CA and
Intermediate CA certificates and \fBssl_verify_client on\fR; the client connects with its private
key and the chain file.
.SH EXAMPLE
.RS
.nf
smi-pki-do-client-cert-request ~/pki acme-billing
smi-upload ~/pki/acme-billing.client.csr incoming/acme-billing.client.csr
.fi
.RE
